    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d595">

                <pb facs="0782" n="688" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg688"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Rockhill to Mr.
                            Taylor.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-10-02"><hi rendition="#italic">October 2,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 581.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Department’s No. 576, of
                    the 24th ultimo, so far as it relates to the claim of Messrs. Bauriedel &amp;
                    Co., agents of certain American tobacco importing houses, to be allowed to
                    export from Cuba tobacco purchased before the date of the Governor-General’s
                    prohibitory decrees, I now inclose copy of a later dispatch<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d595-f1"/> from our consul-general at Habana transmitting the
                    evidence furnished by the claimants to prove their case.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. W. Rockhill</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
